    "title": "Spin Dynamics in Kagome Quantum Spin Liquids",
    "abstract": "Resistance to antimicrobial peptides (AMPs) is a growing global health crisis. To design better therapeutics, we must understand the precise mechanism of membrane insertion. We propose to use Small-Angle Neutron Scattering (SANS) and neutron reflectometry to map the depth-dependent insertion of [Specific Peptide] into a deuterated lipid bilayer. The exceptionally high neutron flux of this facility is required to resolve the low-contrast structural changes occurring during the peptide-membrane binding event at physiological temperatures. These experiments will provide a high-resolution structural map of the pore-formation process, offering a structural template for the development of synthetic, membrane-active drugs.",
